kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-22T12:40:43Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T12:40:43Z","body":"Strange, I'm not sure what could have done that in the SDL update, so we might need to ask the SDL developers if Steam Deck controls work with SDL 3.4.16 outside of Godot.\nFor completeness sake, may I ask if you're running the builds from the \"Steam Big Picture\" mode or from the desktop mode?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5776681416/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5777746602","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123704#issuecomment-5777746602","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123704","id":5777746602,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWGFqqg","user":{"login":"markdigitalue","id":195756432,"node_id":"U_kgDOC6sBkA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195756432?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue","html_url":"https://github.com/markdigitalue","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdigitalue/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-22T13:51:29Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T13:51:29Z","body":"> Strange, I'm not sure what could have done that in the SDL update, so we might need to ask the SDL developers if Steam Deck controls work with SDL 3.4.16 outside of Godot. For completeness sake, may I ask if you're running the builds from the \"Steam Big Picture\" mode or from the desktop mode?\n\nHey there,\n\nI’m running it in the Steam Deck’s default Gaming Mode, which I believe is effectively the Big Picture interface.\n\nI just switched the Steam Deck over to Desktop Mode and launched the game directly from the SteamOS/Arch Linux desktop environment, and the built-in controls worked correctly there.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5777746602/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5900017091","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123704#issuecomment-5900017091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123704","id":5900017091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABX6sdww","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T22:08:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T22:08:58Z","body":"Putting this here for now:\n\nI just had an issue with the in-editor hover hint not being shown anymore which I bisected to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120373 as well.\n\nIt then occurred to me that I still had a steam controller plugged in (direct cable connection not via puck). I then stopped the steam client (not big picture) retried and the issue was still present. After that I unplugged the controller which solved the issue. Plugging it back in I haven't been able to reproduce it since, my best guess is that it is related to the PC entering deep sleep and being reawakened.\n\n<sub>Godot v4.8.dev (af481fd22) - Fedora Linux 44 (Workstation Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor (2560x1440 @ 74.89 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7600 (RADV NAVI33) - AMD Ryzen 7 7700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 30.45 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)</sub>\n\nSo this SDL update seems to be messing with steam hardware beyond steam deck.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5900017091/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5904893879","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123704#issuecomment-5904893879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123704","id":5904893879,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABX_WHtw","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T05:42:36Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T05:42:36Z","body":"I think I know how to fix the issue, I will make a PR to test soon.\nHere's the code that was used to check if a Steam virtual gamepad should be ignored before the update PR:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/28db2de289b3eb8dbc193b9fa5fdf012aed12da7/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/SDL_gamepad.c#L2728-L2737\nIt uses `SDL_GetHintBoolean`, which should be using `SDL_GetEnvironmentVariable` that we fixed for Godot\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/cd9c5d57fb9795886f3bfed8e2003062e1378178/thirdparty/sdl/stdlib/SDL_getenv.c#L158-L162\nHere's this code after the update:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/cd9c5d57fb9795886f3bfed8e2003062e1378178/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/SDL_gamepad.c#L3289-L3299\nIt uses `SDL_getenv_unsafe`, which wasn't fixed for Godot.\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/cd9c5d57fb9795886f3bfed8e2003062e1378178/thirdparty/sdl/stdlib/SDL_getenv.c#L558-L572\n(There's a reason we can't define `HAVE_LIBC_ENVIRONMENT`)\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/cd9c5d57fb9795886f3bfed8e2003062e1378178/drivers/sdl/SDL_build_config_private.h#L91-L95","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5904893879/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]